menu "CrossPad sampler engines"

    config CROSSPAD_SAMPLER_MARCEL
        bool "Build the prebuilt sample streamer beside the native engine"
        default n
        help
            The native engine (crosspad-core src/sampler, SamplerEnginePort.cpp)
            plays every sampler kit. This option builds the prebuilt streamer
            (components/ml_sample_stream_player_lib, main/sample_player_port.cpp's
            library glue, engine_handoff's start/stop, MarcelSampleNode) back in,
            with its own "Sampler" mixer channel and the native engine on
            "Sampler2", so the two can be A/B'd with SMPL_ENGINE native|marcel.

            Off (the default) the image is ~25 kB of code smaller, the arena
            belongs to the native engine from boot, the native engine's mixer
            channel is "Sampler" in the slot the prebuilt one used to have, and
            SMPL_ENGINE answers that only the native engine exists.

endmenu
